{"schemaVersion":1,"framework":"agnostic","version":"v0","id":"skills/jf-naming-conventions","title":"jf-naming-conventions","description":"Find the naming rules for files, symbols, packages, and public APIs.","body":[{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["jf-naming-conventions"]}," keeps vocabulary consistent across source, tests, and documentation. It applies before adding or renaming files, directories, symbols, packages, or APIs."]]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"project-vocabulary-and-defaults"},"children":["Project vocabulary and defaults"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["The agent inspects neighboring code, package names, and the project glossary first. Established conventions and framework-reserved filenames are preserved. For new projects, the defaults are:"]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:table","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"thead","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"tr","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"th","props":{},"children":["Element"]},{"tag":"th","props":{},"children":["Convention"]},{"tag":"th","props":{},"children":["Example"]}]]}]},{"tag":"tbody","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"tr","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":["Source files and directories"]},{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":["kebab-case"]},{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["skill-discovery.ts"]}]}]]},{"tag":"tr","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":["Functions and variables"]},{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":["camelCase"]},{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["discoverPackageSkills"]}]}]]},{"tag":"tr","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":["Types, classes, and React components"]},{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":["PascalCase"]},{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["SkillDeclaration"]}]}]]},{"tag":"tr","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":["Booleans"]},{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":["Predicate names"]},{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["isInstalled"]},", ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["hasChanges"]}]]}]]},{"tag":"tr","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":["npm packages"]},{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":["Lowercase kebab-case"]},{"tag":"td","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["@jfdevelops/skills"]}]}]]}]]}]]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[["Functions describe an action and result. Types use meaningful domain nouns instead of generic suffixes such as ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["Data"]}," or ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["Manager"]},". Filenames use their enclosing context: ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["skills/discover.ts"]}," rather than ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["skills/discover-skills.ts"]},". Role suffixes such as ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":[".test.ts"]}," follow the project's conventions."]]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[["The ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["@jfdevelops/"]}," scope applies to packages intended for that scope; consuming projects keep their own scope. Shared jfdevelops convention skills use the ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["jf-"]}," prefix, with a directory matching the frontmatter name."]]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"rename-coverage"},"children":["Rename coverage"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["A rename includes imports, public entry points, tests, documentation, and configuration references. Public API and import-path compatibility changes must be identified explicitly. The skill does not call for unrelated renames when adopted by an existing project."]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"example-request"},"children":["Example request"]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:pre","props":{"className":"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","style":{"--shiki-light":"#24292e","--shiki-dark":"#e1e4e8","--shiki-light-b